<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="TanMenu.Wpf.Views.Settings.UpdatesCard">
  <!-- One settings row: 更新状态. See the "row spec's shared classes" block in
       Themes/Fluent2/Launcher.axaml for the anatomy, and AppearanceCard's code-behind for the full
       ReloadFromConfig contract every settings card group follows.

       Round 5 rebuilt this group from two cards to one, for the two defects the user screenshotted.

       (1) THE STATUS CARD HAD NO TITLE. Its only Grid.Column="1" child was UpdateStatusText, the dynamic
       status sentence, wearing tm-card-title — inherited from SettingsWindow's 更新 tab, which had no
       title there either. A row whose heading changes from "正在等待检查更新。" to "更新失败：…" is not a
       heading, and the card read as a floating paragraph rather than as a settings row. It now has a
       static title (AppLanguage's UpdateStatusTitle) with the sentence demoted to the subtitle, which is
       also what puts its icon and its buttons on the same y as every other row's.

       (2) 当前版本 IS GONE FROM THIS GROUP. It was an information card with no control sitting in an
       action group, and its version line would have been shown a second time one card apart once 关于
       moved into 设置 — so the version moved to the 关于 card (Views/Settings/AboutCard.axaml, added by
       part C) and the channel-specific help line (UpdatePortableHelp / UpdateStoreManaged /
       UpdateUnavailable, chosen in the code-behind) moved onto this card's expansion row, where it
       explains the status above it. That card carried the 设置 page's only &#xE946;, so the page no
       longer paints it — but the GLYPH IS NOT FREE: Controls/InfoBar.axaml still ships it. (Part B's
       revision of this note also named MainWindow.axaml's NavAboutItem rail row as a consumer; part C
       deleted that row with the rest of the 关于 overlay, so InfoBar is the last one.) Do not re-use the
       glyph for something else here.

       The two buttons are two, so the row spec trails them in column 2 rather than putting them on the
       expansion row; that is what fixes the lone disabled 检查更新 floating at the card's bottom-left.
       The ProgressBar shares the expansion row with the help line and stays IsVisible="False" except
       while downloading.

       Icon: &#xE896; is the exact glyph AppPage's update-notice banner uses, reused here so both update
       entry points read as the same feature. -->
  <StackPanel>
    <TextBlock x:Name="GroupHead" Classes="tm-group-head" />

    <Border Classes="tm-card">
      <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto">
        <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Classes="tm-icon tm-card-icon" Text="&#xE896;" />
        <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Classes="tm-card-text">
          <TextBlock x:Name="UpdateStatusTitle" Classes="tm-card-title" />
          <TextBlock x:Name="UpdateStatusText" Classes="tm-card-sub" />
        </StackPanel>
        <!-- CheckUpdateBtn (检查更新) is a neutral, idempotent check, so it stays on the plain TmButton
             even on its own. UpdateActionBtn (下载更新/重启更新) is the forward-moving action once one
             is available, and gets TmAccentButton — same criteria as PinTaskbarBtn's comment in
             BehaviorCard.axaml. -->
        <StackPanel Grid.Column="2" Classes="tm-card-actions">
          <Button x:Name="CheckUpdateBtn" Theme="{StaticResource TmButton}"
                  Click="OnCheckUpdateClick" />
          <Button x:Name="UpdateActionBtn" Theme="{StaticResource TmAccentButton}"
                  Click="OnUpdateActionClick" IsVisible="False" />
        </StackPanel>
        <StackPanel Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" Classes="tm-card-expander">
          <TextBlock x:Name="UpdateHelpText" Classes="tm-card-sub" />
          <ProgressBar x:Name="UpdateProgress" Height="4" Minimum="0" Maximum="100" IsVisible="False" />
        </StackPanel>
      </Grid>
    </Border>
  </StackPanel>
</UserControl>
